 {"id":"fabro-d9f0","title":"Classify user aborts and sandbox deaths as cancellation, not deterministic failure","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:24:37.527Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:24:37.527Z","description":"In run 01M0QJ5FNE9XZJ72YN31K3X451, implementer@2's termination on user request ('beende den run') plus Docker 409 (container not running) was recorded with category: deterministic and entered loop_failure_signatures, polluting the failure ledger with an interruption that is not a defect. Change: in the workflow engine's failure classification (fabro-workflow), give user-abort/sandbox-death a distinct cancellation category; interim: in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md, route user-stop as 'interrupted' rather than Blocked. Expected effect: failure signatures stay meaningful and retry/health metrics stop counting operator stops as reproducible failures. No existing seed matches (searched deterministic failure, cancellation, failure signature, user abort; fabro-ca74 covers CLI lifecycle commands, a different mechanism).","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-4601","title":"Tell the implementer to edit one file sequentially, never as parallel batches","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:30:20.935Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:30:20.935Z","description":"Add one line to the output-hygiene section of prompts/implementer.md: multiple edits to the same file must be issued sequentially, or the final content emitted once via write_file. Evidence from run 01M0QTNF6GWHGPKHSQ2Y2PB8CQ: worker log 17:31:51 shows six WARN fabro_agent::write_locks: concurrent write to the same file in one batch; serializing events when the implementer fired ~6 parallel edit_file calls at fib_test.go — all serialized into wasted tool round trips. Expected effect: fewer wasted tool round trips per implementer stage and the lock warnings disappear from run logs. Distinct from open fabro-0bfd (engine-side log-count rendering) and closed fabro-facd (harness clobber fix): this is prompt-side prevention.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-0da8","title":"Add a deterministic tracker guard node before the planner","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:35:40.076Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:35:40.076Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro add a script node after start that runs sd list (default output is OPEN issues only, which includes blocked-open seeds — sd ready alone lists unblocked only and would misroute per fabro-aa3d) and sd list --status in_progress; when both are empty, route Tracker empty directly to exit, else continue to planner. Grounded in run 01M0SFEYVC9TD6MP816RHEBFQY: planner@1 spent 27.7s wall / 25.4s inference / $0.0186 (events seq 40-55) solely to discover what ~1.3s of shell proves (6 closed seeds, 0 open). All existing planner-call-economy seeds (fabro-1399, fabro-b382, fabro-e4fa, fabro-aa3d) are prompt edits; none moves the empty-tracker check out of the agent. Expected effect: the common drained-tracker terminal case costs zero agent tokens; planner only runs when there is something to plan.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-9b33","title":"Document sd list read semantics in the planner prompt","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:35:45.618Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:35:45.618Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md, extend the tracker mechanics with: sd list without --status returns OPEN issues only; valid --status values are open|in_progress|closed (there is no all); sd list --status closed confirms the tracker is readable and drained. Grounded in run 01M0SFEYVC9TD6MP816RHEBFQY: the planner's reasoning (event seq 46) doubted whether count=0 meant open-only, probed sd list --status all (seq 48), got a CLI error, and burned one wasted ~7s LLM round-trip before routing Tracker empty. Complements open fabro-1399 (which covers write syntax and call order, not read-flag semantics). Expected effect: one fewer inference turn per planner invocation and faster correct Tracker-empty routing.","labels":["revision"]}
